mhvtl-control for Debian
=================

mhvtl-control is installed but neither enabled nor started. To run it:

  systemctl enable --now mhvtl-control

It listens on http://127.0.0.1:8080 by default. Options, including the
listen address, an API token and TLS, are set in /etc/mhvtl/mhvtl-control.env
(mode 0600); restart mhvtl-control after changing it. mhvtl-control refuses to bind a
non-loopback address without a token.

mhvtl-control finds mhVTL's libraries in /etc/mhvtl/device.conf and talks to the
running mhVTL daemons, so it is useful once the mhvtl package is set up.
It tolerates mhVTL starting after it, and mhVTL restarts.
